  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Then the number of possible functions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>S</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>S</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>S</mi></math>, is equal to _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "490",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can be any value between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Similarly&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can take any value from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, total number of function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>490</mn></math></p>"
  }
